@using ContentManagementSystem.Core.Delivery.Seo
@* Everything spec section 18.2 puts in the head of a public page, written from a metadata record
   that has already resolved it. There is no fallback logic here and no query: this component is a
   loop, deliberately, so that "what does this page emit" is answered by SeoMetadataBuilder alone
   rather than by two halves that can disagree.

   The JSON-LD blocks are written as raw markup, element and all. That is safe here and nowhere
   else: every document was produced by System.Text.Json with the default encoder, which escapes the
   angle brackets that could otherwise close the element. The element itself is raw because the
   component renderer HTML-encodes attribute values — it would emit the type as
   application/ld&#x2B;json, which every conformant parser decodes and not every crawler's does. *@
<title>@Metadata.Title</title>
@if (Metadata.Description is { Length: > 0 } description)
{
    <meta name="description" content="@description" />
}
<link rel="canonical" href="@Metadata.CanonicalUrl" />
<meta name="robots" content="@Metadata.Robots" />
@foreach (var tag in Metadata.Meta)
{
    @if (tag.Attribute == SeoMetaTag.PropertyAttribute)
    {
        <meta property="@tag.Key" content="@tag.Content" />
    }
    else
    {
        <meta name="@tag.Key" content="@tag.Content" />
    }
}
@foreach (var script in Metadata.JsonLd)
{
    @((MarkupString)$"<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{script}</script>")
}
